The size-6 X-coalition (ℓ=3 on {x1,x2,x3}) does force |W ∩ X| ≥ 2, which already secures the lower bound of two approvals for voter 1. The size-4 Y-coalition (ℓ=2 on {y4,y5,y6}) only requires two seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}. That quota is met by any single y4–y6 candidate paired with z1 (or z2), which uses just two of the five seats. The remaining three seats can then be filled with two X-candidates plus both y1 and z3.  

