All A-style constructions attempting four approvals (e.g., \(\{x_1,x_2,y_1,z_3,y_4\}\) or \(\{x_1,x_2,x_3,y_1,y_4\}\)) necessarily displace one of the required Y/Z seats and thereby leave the size-4 Y-coalition (or its sub-coalitions) with at most one approved member; they are therefore invalid. The explicit realizing committees already identified—\(\{x_1,x_2,z_1,y_4,y_5\}\) (=2) and \(\{x_1,x_2,x_3,y_4,y_5\}\) (=3)—meet both quotas simultaneously. Hence the attainable interval is exactly [2,3] (choice H).

