Round-3 public messages confirm attainable interval exactly [2,3] (H). Explicit witnesses: {x1,x2,z1,y4,y5} (|W ∩ A1|=2) and {x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} (|W ∩ A1|=3). Majority (cols 1,3,4,6,7,10–12,15–18) repeatedly shows 4 impossible: any attempt adding both y1+z3 displaces a required Y/Z seat, leaving Sy or voters 8–10 short. A-claims (cols 2,5,8,9,13,14) rely on z1 + single y4–6 satisfying Sy quota, but fail explicit counter-examples (e.g., voters 8–10 receive only 2 approvals; sub-coalition violations persist; z1 substitution does not free an extra A1 slot without quota breach).

No new evidence alters prior conclusion; A constructions recycle refuted patterns. Attainable range remains precisely min 2, max 3 (choice H).}

1.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H. min 2, max 3

The two dominant EJR constraints remain decisive and unchanged: the size-6 ℓ=3 X-coalition forces |W ∩ X| ≥ 2 (hence ≥2 approvals for voter 1), while the size-4 ℓ=2 Y-coalition forces ≥2 seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}. With |W|=5 the latter quota leaves at most three seats that can intersect A1, so |W ∩ A1|≤3. Both bounds are tight, as witnessed by the explicit EJR-satisfying committees already enumerated multiple times: {x1,x2,z1,y4,y5} (=2) and {x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} (=3).

All A constructions that attempt four approvals necessarily displace at least one required Y/Z seat (explicit counter-example: any set containing both y1 and z3 plus two X-candidates gives voters 4–7 at most one approved member). No new sub-coalition or counter-example evades this. Persistent: H correct, A refuted on seat-counting + explicit failure. Unresolved: none.}

4.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H. min 2, max 3

The dominant EJR quotas are unchanged and decisive. The size-6 ℓ=3 X-coalition on {x1,x2,x3} forces |W ∩ X| ≥ 2, already securing the lower bound of two approvals for voter 1; any committee with |W ∩ X| ≤ 1 leaves voters 8–10 (and the size-5 sub-coalition) below threshold. The size-4 ℓ=2 Y-coalition on {y4,y5,y6} simultaneously forces at least two seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}; with |W|=5 this quota leaves at most three seats intersecting A1 = {x1,x2,x3,y1,z3}, ruling out four or more.

Explicit EJR committees realize both endpoints:  
- {x1,x2,z1,y4,y5} meets every threshold and yields exactly two approvals for voter 1;  
- {x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} meets every threshold and yields exactly three approvals for voter 1.  

All constructions offered for four approvals (e.g., {x1,x2,y1,z3,y4}, {x1,x2,z1,y4,y1}) necessarily leave at least one voter in {4,5,6,7} with only a single approved member once the two required Y/Z seats are seated, violating the second quota. No new sub-coalition or cohesiveness argument has been supplied that evades these seat-counting facts. The attainable interval remains exactly [2,3].}

